    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27695" root="ظن" body-key="Z">
    
      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التَّظَنِّى</span></b>  means <i>The exercising, employing,</i> or
<i>using, of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الظَّنّ</span> [i. e. <i>thought,</i> &amp;c.]; originally
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التَّظَنُّنُ</span>. (S, K.) A'Obeyd says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَظَنَّيْتُ</span> is from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَنَنْتُ</span>, and is originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَظَنَّنْتُ</span>; the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ن</span> being
many, one of them is changed into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span>: it is like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصَّيْتُ</span>, which is originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَصَّصْتُ</span>. (T.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See
also 1, first sentence.

